Z||000000||jerpro||11-18-2000||04:01 PM||||anyone have any previos experience with the company pisa corp.? The front of my 2m4 just got pinned under a bmw z3 (if you're going to crash in the winter do it right). The front bumper is in ok shape and is fixable, but I want to take this opportunity to change it for the new euro bumper. <BR>Are they a good company? <BR>OR any other suggestions?<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/euroff.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cybercars.com/mnfr/fierohq/euroff.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||11-18-2000||04:34 PM||||  I haven't bought anything from PISA yet, but I have had the opportunity to talk with them over the phone on some project ideas that I had. They are very honest and willing to help in any way. Like I said I haven't purchased any of their products yet, but I don't feel like I would hesitate to. If you have any questions, give them a call and you will see what I mean.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
