Z||000003||Zorba||11-18-2000||06:32 PM|||| Pay for stuff in full then wait for them to send it out so someone else can make it so they can ship it to you. Nothing in stock, ever. But they make good products. If you are the impatient type and need things within a week. FORGET IT&gt;||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-18-2000||11:36 PM||||I to havent ever purchased anything from them, but have heard that their "replacement" wrap around dashes are not good quality at all. They have to be trimed and modified to go in the Fiero. I would call them and see if you cant talk to some people who have purcheased and installed the product your talking about.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||11-18-2000||11:40 PM||||i bought 1 thing from pisa...that was the "big fiero book" or whatever.  it has all kinds of stuff from different companies.  it took about 3 weeks to get here.  i called there once to purchase that euro bumper, but changed my mind.  the guy sounded nice and was very helpful.  well there's my advice or whatever.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||11-18-2000||11:48 PM||||One of the guys in our club (Georgia Fieros) bought the Artero body kit and installed it on his SE. He was very satisfied with his purchase, and the support that PISA provided.<P>If your interested in seeing the build process, click... <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=236420&a=1757825" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=236420&a=1757825</A> <P>The pics don't do justice to the finished product. It's absolutely flawless.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierov8||11-19-2000||12:10 AM||||jerpro,<P>Where to begin, where to begin......<P>Firstoff -- IF you want the 355 nose, DO NOT get it from PISA.  Get it from Denny Patton at the geocities link shown above.  PISA has an early generation mold of the 355 nose from Denny.  I think Denny is selling a 3rd or 4th generation part.  Denny's fiberglass quality is OUTSTANDINGLY GOOD!!!  I have a set of his side scoops and am extremely satisfied with them -- they only need a minor scuffing and paint -- they even came with a gelcoat finish.<P>Now, on to PISA....<P>I have a ZR-2 dash in my car (go to photopoint.com and look at my pics at email address fierov8@tensor.com).  Contrary to PISA's estimate that it takes about 8 hours to install their dash, I think no one task I did took 8 hours.  Granted, I did change a few things (used VDO gauges in a custom set of aluminum panels), but I did spend considerable hours making things fit, cutting and remolding warped sections, etc. Spent a bunch of time just making the dash and console fit together.  The glass quality was really poor -- just glad I could cover it up with foam and vinyl!<P>I also ordered a Haynes manual from them separate from my ZR2 dash.  Took several calls and a threat to cancel the order -- all of a sudden, they "found" one to send out right away.<P>The above was about 2.5 years or so ago.  Recently (last May) I placed an order for their GT taillight kit.  Waited almost 6 weeks -- no parts.  Placed several calls in that time, got excuses why the parts weren't ready.  The last time I called and cancelled the order, Dan C. (owner) starts to backpedal and asks me not to cancel, that they can ship everything out the next day (???).  Funny how at the start of the call I was told that it would be another 1-2 weeks!  I said thanks, but no, just credit my card, thank you very much.  <P>Just my experience, HTH, YMMV, etc.<P>-jeff d<BR>Fort Worth, TX||||reg||1
Z||000008||Zorba||11-20-2000||12:42 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by fierov8:<BR>[B]jerpro,<P>Where to begin, where to begin......<P>Firstoff -- IF you want the 355 nose, DO NOT get  <P>Seller:<BR>My philosophy on doing business: IF YOU DON'T Make the part, don't advertise that you DO. IF it takes 3-4 weeks for delivery, disclose it. If it takes 8 weeks. Disclose it. If you are out of stock, disclose it.<P>Buyer: Use your credit card only. Period. If you send cash, you are stuck. If you get the wrong product you are stuck. For example one time a sent $200.00 for a set of Testarossa front lights for my (sold) kitcar. On the phone the description of the product sounded great. 2 weeks later I get the parts: cheap plastic garbage worth about $20.00 a piece at the most. Most reputable companies will take a credit card. I only send money to people I personally know. Period.<BR>Buy only from reputable companies and catalogs. IF you hear 2-3 bad experiences about one company, stay away, you are likely to become the 4th bad experience story.<BR>2 cents.||||reg||12
Z||000009||BAM-BAM||11-20-2000||10:33 AM||||  When I inquired from PISA about the ZR2 dash I was told, by PISA, that it wasn't a good quality product and that unless I was doing a kit car or absolutely wanted it to try something else. They also explained to me that the time estimate may be a little on the conservative side and to expect to spend more than 8 hours on install. As for the quality of there products, I can't say. Like I said before, I am intent on some of there products, ZR2 hood cowl and front section possibly. This come with great recomendation from Forum members who have delt with PISA in the past year or so. So, like I said before, give a call and talk to them. Then "YOU" can decide weather or not to trust them. Be sure and ask them about the quality of there workmanship. Time goes by and people and buisnesses learn. We are not all perfect in the begining.<P><BR>  Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||9
